    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0470" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1948v01p1/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Armaments/10–748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of State,
                        in Paris</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-07T19:00:00-05:00">October 7, 1948—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Gadel 147. Dept has reservations re del decision Oct. 1, on handling Soviet
                    disarmament proposal as reported Delga 187, Oct. 2, 9 a. m.,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d245-f1"/> and desires consult Secretary on his return here Oct. 9.
                    Accordingly you should endeavor not to participate in disarmament debate in
                    Committee <pb facs="0471" n="451" xml:id="pg451"/> 1 pending further
                    instructions. For your most secret info Dept wonders whether from propaganda
                    point of view some more affirmative response to Soviet proposals might not be
                    made.</p>
                <p>In view of fact that tomorrow will be devoted to plenary session we are hopeful
                    that our non-participation in debate can be contrived inconspiciously.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d245-f1" n="1" xml:id="d245-f1-content">
                <p> Delga 187, not printed, reported the decisions taken by the Delegation at its
                    10th Meeting, October 1; for the pertinent portion of the Minutes of that
                    meeting, see <ref target="#pg443">p. 443</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
